<title>POLAND: Polish T-bill minimum prices ease at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish T-bill minimum prices ease at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of the 39-week and the 26-week Polish T-bills both eased at Wednesday's primary auction on total demand of 499 million zlotys against a 600 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold 336 million zlotys worth of bills.</p>
<p>The ministry will offer 1.4 billion bills at a primary auction on Monday, June 16.  </p>
